{:edb/db-before-t 886 :edb/db-after-t 887 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534199 50 #inst "2026-10-06T10:10:21.722Z" 13194139534199 true] [17592186096527 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281877 13194139534199 true] [17592186096527 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281886 13194139534199 true] [17592186096529 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281881 13194139534199 true] [17592186096529 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281893 13194139534199 true] [17592186096530 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281874 13194139534199 true] [17592186281874 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281875 13194139534199 true] [17592186281874 1089 "q-274608" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281874 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534199 true] [17592186281874 1100 "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281874 1113 #uuid "c890a749-89bd-5f7a-8848-aae7a952ef6b" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281874 1145 "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(2)^{2}+(5)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+25 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =29 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281876 13194139534199 true] [17592186281875 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534199 true] [17592186281875 1041 "field-1" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281875 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281876 13194139534199 true] [17592186281875 1110 #uuid "bb86c23b-2ad0-5c04-87a3-d219eb6377b7" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281876 1034 "\\sqrt{29}" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281876 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281876 1111 #uuid "276e148f-0b35-5396-a427-5625a3fbc2ef" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281877 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281878 13194139534199 true] [17592186281877 1089 "q-327723" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281877 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534199 true] [17592186281877 1100 "Given that the expression $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the **exact** value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($ \n{{field-1}} $)$" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281877 1113 #uuid "855c97cf-010b-5c84-8d20-2273c5c0a4d2" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281877 1145 "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281879 13194139534199 true] [17592186281878 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281880 13194139534199 true] [17592186281878 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534199 true] [17592186281878 1041 "field-1" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281878 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281880 13194139534199 true] [17592186281878 1110 #uuid "5261daf7-2e11-5371-b298-a3a1783a92a2" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281879 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281879 1111 #uuid "f98025fc-aa81-5dec-81bd-9f432e1ffcac" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281880 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281880 1111 #uuid "28ce03b8-392b-50fd-a2c4-578ecab26b4b" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281881 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281882 13194139534199 true] [17592186281881 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281884 13194139534199 true] [17592186281881 1089 "q-327982" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281881 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534199 true] [17592186281881 1100 "Express $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Use the **exact value** for $R,$ and round $ϕ$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n$5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$)$" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281881 1113 #uuid "71d47ce5-da63-5fd4-a040-f991c91be8f9" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281881 1145 "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude–phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ ϕ & =arctan\\,(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\ ϕ & ≈0.381\\,\\text{rad},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nFor the amplitude,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ & ={2}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+25 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =29 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)≈\\sqrt{29}sin\\,(x-0.381).\n$$" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281883 13194139534199 true] [17592186281882 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534199 true] [17592186281882 1041 "field-1" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281882 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281883 13194139534199 true] [17592186281882 1110 #uuid "015e8759-b0e1-55c9-8bee-20101d2f06a3" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281883 1034 "\\sqrt{29}" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281883 1111 #uuid "6bf49106-353a-5c48-97c4-220a494985c8" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281885 13194139534199 true] [17592186281884 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534199 true] [17592186281884 1041 "field-2" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281884 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281885 13194139534199 true] [17592186281884 1110 #uuid "cbe94955-29c5-52cc-a713-bbd150fc22c3" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281885 1034 "0.381" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281885 1111 #uuid "291b63a1-c462-5e75-ab6e-3fc4a5607f78" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281886 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281887 13194139534199 true] [17592186281886 1089 "q-80133" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281886 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534199 true] [17592186281886 1100 "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281886 1113 #uuid "9dc5cfec-844b-5c04-a039-53f657410565" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281886 1145 "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =5 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281888 13194139534199 true] [17592186281887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281889 13194139534199 true] [17592186281887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281890 13194139534199 true] [17592186281887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281891 13194139534199 true] [17592186281887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281892 13194139534199 true] [17592186281887 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534199 true] [17592186281887 1041 "selection" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281887 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281888 13194139534199 true] [17592186281887 1110 #uuid "db73b152-d743-5e5a-9775-99aef07dfeb6" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281888 1034 "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5)" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281888 1111 #uuid "43ebdc72-c722-5f07-ae01-db469ae6b665" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281889 1034 "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281889 1111 #uuid "ca6a4fb8-2db0-59c7-8419-506b1942ff19" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281890 1034 "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281890 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281890 1111 #uuid "bbcf352f-f2e7-5324-bb0d-d84ac79366d3" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281891 1034 "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281891 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281891 1111 #uuid "e9fb57c0-f43d-5c26-b6e3-6af15bbdc903" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281892 1034 "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(10)" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281892 1111 #uuid "a45bb909-9087-5874-b23d-51114a3e7825" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281893 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281894 13194139534199 true] [17592186281893 1089 "q-80147" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281893 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534199 true] [17592186281893 1100 "$2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)≈$" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281893 1113 #uuid "da754d54-7ad0-5021-82bb-f04c6fa332b7" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281893 1145 "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =0.955\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =8+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =24 \\\\ R & =2\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)\n$$" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281895 13194139534199 true] [17592186281894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281896 13194139534199 true] [17592186281894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281897 13194139534199 true] [17592186281894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281898 13194139534199 true] [17592186281894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281899 13194139534199 true] [17592186281894 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534199 true] [17592186281894 1041 "selection" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281894 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281895 13194139534199 true] [17592186281894 1110 #uuid "3d3a0c80-1834-5558-a1e9-38a21bc6e1be" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281895 1034 "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281895 1111 #uuid "fe968fbe-d97d-504c-b62e-527278272744" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281896 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-1.156)" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281896 1111 #uuid "c7f0e66f-9dfb-5d78-b659-a4fae80d7f1f" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281897 1034 "\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.854)" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281897 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281897 1111 #uuid "c74cb847-af86-546c-a94c-daee7590d07d" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281898 1034 "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.916)" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281898 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281898 1111 #uuid "5df9f194-a06d-5fe6-a71d-aa94e6598893" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281899 1034 "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-1.054)" 13194139534199 true] [17592186281899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534199 true] [17592186281899 1111 #uuid "79bca67